#: lib/installer.php
msgid "Cacti needs to establish network connections, execute binaries and write files to work. Linux security features such as <b>SELinux</b>, <b>AppArmor</b> or <b>ModSecurity</b> may cause Cacti to become inoperable in some configurations. If problems occur, check the settings of these security tools.<br/><br/>"
msgstr "Cacti kwesịrị iguzobe njikọ netwọkụ, mee ka faịlụ baịnarị rụọ ọrụ ma dee faịlụ iji rụọ ọrụ. Atụmatụ nchekwa Linux dịka <b>SELinux</b>, <b>AppArmor</b> ma ọ bụ <b>ModSecurity</b> nwere ike ime ka Cacti ghara ịrụ ọrụ na nhazi ụfọdụ. Ọ bụrụ na nsogbu adị, lelee ntọala nke ngwaọrụ nchekwa ndị a.<br/><br/>"

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "Input Validation Whitelist Protection"
msgstr "Nchedo Ndepụta Nkwenye Nyocha Ntinye"

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "Cacti Data Input methods that call a script can be exploited in ways that a non-administrator can perform damage to either files owned by the poller account, and in cases where someone runs the Cacti poller as root, can compromise the operating system allowing attackers to exploit your infrastructure."
msgstr "Enwere ike iji ụzọ Ntinye Data Cacti nke na-akpọ edemede mee ihe n'ụzọ ọjọọ nke na onye na-abụghị onye nchịkwa nwere ike imebi faịlụ nke akaụntụ onye nyocha nwe, yana n'ọnọdụ ebe mmadụ na-eji root arụ ọrụ onye nyocha Cacti, ọ nwere ike imebi sistemụ arụmọrụ ma mee ka ndị mwakpo wakpo akụrụngwa gị."

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "Therefore, several versions ago, Cacti was enhanced to provide Whitelist capabilities on the these types of Data Input Methods.  Though this does secure Cacti more thoroughly, it does increase the amount of work required by the Cacti administrator to import and manage Templates and Packages."
msgstr "Ya mere, ọtụtụ ụdị gara aga, e kwalitere Cacti iji nye ikike Ndepụta Nkwenye n'ụdị Ụzọ Ntinye Data ndị a. Ọ bụ ezie na nke a na-echebe Cacti nke ọma karị, ọ na-abawanye ọrụ dịịrị onye nchịkwa Cacti iji bubata ma jikwaa Ndetu na Ngwugwu."

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "The way that the Whitelisting works is that when you first import a Data Input Method, or you re-import a Data Input Method, and the script and or arguments change in any way, the Data Input Method, and all the corresponding Data Sources will be immediately disabled until the administrator validates that the Data Input Method is valid."
msgstr "Otu Ndepụta Nkwenye si arụ ọrụ bụ na mgbe ị bubatara Ụzọ Ntinye Data nke mbụ, ma ọ bụ mgbe ị bubataghachiri Ụzọ Ntinye Data, ma edemede ahụ na ma ọ bụ arụmụka gbanwee n'ụzọ ọ bụla, a ga-agbanyụ Ụzọ Ntinye Data ahụ na Isi Data niile kwekọrọ ozugbo ruo mgbe onye nchịkwa kwadoro na Ụzọ Ntinye Data ahụ dị mma."

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "To make identifying Data Input Methods in this state, we have provided a validation script in Cacti's CLI directory that can be run with the following options:"
msgstr "Iji mee ka ịchọpụta Ụzọ Ntinye Data n'ọnọdụ a dị mfe, anyị enyela edemede nkwenye na ndekọ CLI nke Cacti nke enwere ike iji nhọrọ ndị a mee:"

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "This script option will search for any Data Input Methods that are currently banned and provide details as to why."
msgstr "Nhọrọ edemede a ga-achọ Ụzọ Ntinye Data ọ bụla a machibidoro iwu ugbu a ma nye nkọwa maka ihe kpatara ya."

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "This script option un-ban the Data Input Methods that are currently banned."
msgstr "Nhọrọ edemede a na-ewepụ mmachibido iwu na Ụzọ Ntinye Data ndị a machibidoro iwu ugbu a."

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "This script option will re-enable any disabled Data Sources."
msgstr "Nhọrọ edemede a ga-emeghachi Isi Iyi Data ọ bụla agbanyụrụ agbanyụ."

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "It is strongly suggested that you update your config.php to enable this feature by uncommenting the <b>$input_whitelist</b> variable and then running the three CLI script options above after the web based install has completed.<br/><br/>"
msgstr "A na-atụ aro nke ukwuu ka ị melite config.php gị iji mee ka atụmatụ a rụọ ọrụ site n'iwepụ akara nkọwa na mgbanwe <b>$input_whitelist</b> ma mesịa mee nhọrọ edemede CLI atọ dị n'elu mgbe nrụnye dabere na webụ gachara.<br/><br/>"

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "Check the Checkbox below to acknowledge that you have read and understand this security concern"
msgstr "Kaa akara n'igbe nlele dị n'okpuru iji kweta na ị gụọla ma ghọta nchegbu nchekwa a"

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "I have read this statement"
msgstr "Agụọla m nkwupụta a"

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "Admin email address"
msgstr "Adreesị ozi-e nke onye nchịkwa"

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "In case of problems cacti can send emails to the administrator. The address filled in here will be assigned to the admin account and \"Notify Primary Admin of Issue\" will be enabled. You can change this setting and the email address later. Do not forget to set up the email settings after installation."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na nsogbu adị, Cacti nwere ike izigara onye nchịkwa ozi-e. A ga-ekenye adreesị e dejupụtara ebe a na akaụntụ onye nchịkwa ma gbanye \"Gwa Onye Nchịkwa Mbụ Maka Nsogbu\". Ị nwere ike ịgbanwe ntọala a na adreesị ozi-e emechaa. Echefula ịtọ ntọala ozi-e mgbe nrụnye gachara."

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "Default Profile"
msgstr "Profaịlụ Ndabere"

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "Please select the default Data Source Profile to be used for polling sources. This is the maximum amount of time between scanning devices for information so the lower the polling interval, the more work is placed on the Cacti Server host. Long retention profiles store more data, so they take up more disk capacity. Their advantage is that older data is not as consolidated and is therefore more accurate than using shorter retention."
msgstr "Biko họrọ Profaịlụ Isi Iyi Data ndabere a ga-eji maka ịnakọta data n'isi iyi. Nke a bụ oge kachasị elu dị n'etiti inyocha ngwaọrụ maka ozi, yabụ ka oge nyocha dị mkpụmkpụ, otú ahụ ka ọrụ na-aba ụba na sava Cacti. Profaịlụ njide ogologo oge na-echekwa data karịa, yabụ ha na-ewe ohere diski karịa. Uru ha bụ na a naghị achịkọta data ochie nke ukwuu, ya mere ọ na-enwe eziokwu karịa iji njide dị mkpụmkpụ."

#: lib/installer.php
msgid "Also, select the intended, or configured Cron interval that you wish to use for Data Collection."
msgstr "Ọzọkwa, họrọ oge etiti Cron e zubere ma ọ bụ nke ahaziri nke ịchọrọ iji maka Nchịkọta Data."

