#: login_providers.php
msgid "Should LDAP verify TLS Certificates when received by the Client."
msgstr "Ọ bụrụ na LDAP ga-enyocha Asambodo TLS mgbe onye ahịa (Client) natara ha."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Referrals"
msgstr "Ntụaka (Referrals)"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Enable or Disable LDAP referrals.  If disabled, it may increase the speed of searches."
msgstr "Kwado maọbụ gbanyụọ ntụaka LDAP. Ọ bụrụ na e gbanyụọ ya, ọ nwere ike ime ka nchọta dịkwuo ngwa."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Mode"
msgstr "Ọnọdụ"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Mode which cacti will attempt to authenticate against the LDAP server.<blockquote><i>No Searching</i> - No Distinguished Name (DN) searching occurs, just attempt to bind with the provided Distinguished Name (DN) format.<br><br><i>Anonymous Searching</i> - Attempts to search for username against LDAP directory via anonymous binding to locate the users Distinguished Name (DN).<br><br><i>Specific Searching</i> - Attempts search for username against LDAP directory via Specific Distinguished Name (DN) and Specific Password for binding to locate the users Distinguished Name (DN).<br><br><i>One-Time Passwords (OTP/MFA)</i> - Cacti binds the user password only once, during final authentication.  <i>No Searching</i> performs no directory lookup and binds directly using the Distinguished Name (DN) template, so it is safe for OTP when the DN template alone identifies the user.  When a directory lookup is required to resolve the DN, use <i>Specific Searching</i> with a dedicated service account (or <i>Anonymous Searching</i> where the directory permits it) so the lookup never consumes the single-use code.  For resilient OTP deployments use a single DNS load balancer name in the Server(s) field rather than a space delimited multi-server list, which would re-attempt the bind with an already-consumed one-time password."
msgstr "Ụdị nke Cacti ga-eji chọọ ikwado njirimara na sava LDAP.<blockquote><i>Enweghị Nchọgharị</i> - Enweghị nchọgharị Distinguished Name (DN) ga-eme, naanị gbalịa ijikọ na usoro Distinguished Name (DN) e nyere.<br><br><i>Nchọgharị Na-enweghị Aha</i> - Na-agbalị ịchọ aha njirimara na ndekọ LDAP site na njikọ na-enweghị aha iji chọta Distinguished Name (DN) nke onye ọrụ.<br><br><i>Nchọgharị Kpọmkwem</i> - Na-agbalị ịchọ aha njirimara na ndekọ LDAP site na Specific Distinguished Name (DN) na Okwuntụghe Kpọmkwem maka njikọ iji chọta Distinguished Name (DN) nke onye ọrụ.<br><br><i>Okwuntụghe Otu Ugboro (OTP/MFA)</i> - Cacti na-ejikọ okwuntụghe onye ọrụ naanị otu ugboro, n'oge nkwado ikpeazụ. <i>Enweghị Nchọgharị</i> anaghị eme nchọgharị ndekọ ọ bụla ma na-ejikọ kpọmkwem site na iji ndebiri Distinguished Name (DN), ya mere ọ dị mma maka OTP mgbe ndebiri DN naanị na-akọwa onye ọrụ ahụ. Mgbe a chọrọ nchọgharị ndekọ iji dozie DN ahụ, jiri <i>Nchọgharị Kpọmkwem</i> nwere akaụntụ ọrụ pụrụ iche (ma ọ bụ <i>Nchọgharị Na-enweghị Aha</i> ebe ndekọ ahụ kwere ya) ka nchọgharị ahụ wee ghara iri koodu e ji otu ugboro eme ihe. Maka ntinye OTP siri ike, jiri otu aha nhazi ibu DNS n'ọhịa Server(s) kama ndepụta ọtụtụ sava nke oghere kewara, nke ga-anwa ijikọ ọzọ site na iji okwuntụghe otu ugboro e jirila."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Distinguished Name (DN)"
msgstr "Aha Pụrụ Iche (DN)"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "The \"Distinguished Name\" syntax, applicable for both OpenLDAP and Windows AD configurations, offers flexibility in defining user identity. For OpenLDAP, the format follows this structure: <i>\"uid=&lt;username&gt;,ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>. Windows AD provides an alternative syntax: <i>\"&lt;username&gt;@win2kdomain.local\"</i>, commonly known as \"userPrincipalName (UPN)\". In this context, \"&lt;username&gt;\" represents the specific username provided during the login prompt. This is particularly pertinent when operating in \"No Searching\" mode, or \"Require Group Membership\" enabled."
msgstr "Usoro ederede \"Distinguished Name\", nke dabara maka nhazi OpenLDAP na Windows AD abụọ, na-enye mgbanwe dị mfe n'ịkọwa njirimara onye ọrụ. Maka OpenLDAP, usoro ahụ na-agbaso nhazi a: <i>\"uid=&lt;username&gt;,ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>. Windows AD na-enye usoro ederede ọzọ: <i>\"&lt;username&gt;@win2kdomain.local\"</i>, nke a na-akpọkarị \"userPrincipalName (UPN)\". N'ọnọdụ a, \"&lt;username&gt;\" na-anọchi anya aha njirimara kpọmkwem e nyere n'oge a na-arịọ nbanye. Nke a dị mkpa karịsịa mgbe a na-arụ ọrụ n'ụdị \"Enweghị Nchọgharị\", ma ọ bụ mgbe a kwadoro \"Chọọ Nsonye Otu\"."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "uid=<username>,ou=people,dc=example,dc=com"
msgstr "uid=<username>,ou=people,dc=example,dc=com"

#: login_providers.php user_admin.php
msgid "Group Membership"
msgstr "Ịbụ Onye Otu"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Group Distinguished Name (DN)"
msgstr "Aha Pụrụ Iche (DN) nke Otu"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Distinguished Name of the group that the user must be a member of in order to login. Leave blank to allow any successfully authenticated user to login."
msgstr "Aha Pụrụ Iche nke otu onye ọrụ ga-abụrịrị onye otu ya iji banye. Hapụ ya n'efu iji kwe ka onye ọrụ ọ bụla e kwadoro nke ọma banye."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "ou=cacti-admins,dc=example,dc=com"
msgstr "ou=cacti-admins,dc=example,dc=com"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Group Member Attribute"
msgstr "Njirimara Onye Otu"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "This refers to the specific attribute within the LDAP directory that holds the usernames of group members. It is crucial to ensure that the attribute value aligns with the configuration specified in the \"Distinguished Name\" or that the actual attribute value is searchable using the settings outlined in the \"Distinguished Name\"."
msgstr "Nke a na-ezo aka na njirimara kpọmkwem dị n'ime ndekọ LDAP nke na-ejide aha ndị ọrụ nke ndị otu. Ọ dị oke mkpa ijide n'aka na uru njirimara ahụ kwekọrọ na nhazi e depụtara na \"Aha Pụrụ Iche\" maọbụ na a pụrụ ịchọ uru njirimara ahụ n'ezie site n'iji ntọala e gosipụtara na \"Aha Pụrụ Iche\"."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "memberUid"
msgstr "memberUid"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Group Member Type"
msgstr "Ụdị Onye Otu"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Defines if users use full Distinguished Name or just Username in the defined Group Member Attribute."
msgstr "Na-akọwa ma ndị ọrụ ha na-eji Aha Pụrụ Iche zuru ezu maọbụ naanị Aha Onye Ọrụ na Njirimara Onye Otu a kọwapụtara."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Search Settings"
msgstr "Ntọala Nchọta"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Search Base"
msgstr "Ebe Ntọala Nchọta"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Search base for searching the LDAP directory, such as <i>\"dc=win2kdomain,dc=local\"</i> or <i>\"ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>."
msgstr "Ebe ntọala nchọta maka ịchọ ndekọ LDAP, dị ka <i>\"dc=win2kdomain,dc=local\"</i> maọbụ <i>\"ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "ou=people,dc=example,dc=com"
msgstr "ou=people,dc=example,dc=com"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Search Filter"
msgstr "Ihe Nzacha Nchọta"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Search filter to use to locate the user in the LDAP directory, such as for windows: <i>\"(&amp;(objectclass=user)(objectcategory=user)(userPrincipalName=&lt;username&gt;*))\"</i> or for OpenLDAP: <i>\"(&(objectClass=account)(uid=&lt;username&gt))\"</i>.  \"&lt;username&gt\" is replaced with the username that was supplied at the login prompt."
msgstr "Nzacha ọchụchọ a ga-eji chọta onye ọrụ na ndekọ LDAP, dịka maka windows: <i>\"(&amp;(objectclass=user)(objectcategory=user)(userPrincipalName=&lt;username&gt;*))\"</i> ma ọ bụ maka OpenLDAP: <i>\"(&(objectClass=account)(uid=&lt;username&gt))\"</i>.  A na-eji aha onye ọrụ e nyere n'ebe mbanye dochie \"&lt;username&gt\"."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "(&(objectClass=account)(uid=<username>))"
msgstr "(&(objectClass=account)(uid=<username>))"

